i 9918917720506676DNLM20251117104513.0211110s2022    fr ac    b    001 0 fre    a  2022430606  a9782759826780q(paperback)  a2759826783q(paperback)  a(OCoLC)1329224140  aERASPbengerdacDLCdLGGdOCLCFdPULdERASPdOCLCOdIG#  alccopycat  9France00aRA643b.C37 202200aWC 11.104a610.91 aCavaillon, Jean-Marc,eauthor.13aLe mauvais air :bil était une fois les infections et les combattants de l'ombre /cJean-Marc Cavaillon. 1aLes Ulis :bEDP Sciences,c[2022]  a432 pages :billustrations, portraits ;c21 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.00tÀ propos de l'Auteur --tPréambule --tPandémies et épidémies --tAussi loin que l'homme se souvienne --tLe mauvais air --tLes miasmes --tDe l'intuition aux découvertes --tL'affrontement entre contagionnistes et anticontagionnistes --tDémonstration de la contagiosité sur soi-même --tAu-delà des animalcules --tLes premiers microscopistes --tFermentation alcoolique --tGénération spontanée et réfutation --tDes germes aux maladies infectieuses --tVers la théorie des germes --tL'anthrax --tLa tuberculose --tLa coqueluche --tStreptocoque et staphylocoque --tLe typhus --tLa syphilis --tMaladies infectieuses et folie --tLes infections parasitaires --tDes germes aux toxines --tLes poisons vénériens --tLes poisons bactériens --tLes exotoxines --tGermes et auto-intoxications --tDes virus aux infections virales --tD'un terme latin a un nom contemporain --tLa rage --tLa grippe --tLe COVID-19 --tLa lutte contre les maladies infectieuses --tL'herbologie --tLes antiseptiques --tLes antibiotiques --tLes bactériophages --tL'hygiène --tLes masques --tLes vaccins --tLa variolisation --tLa syphilisation --tLa vaccination --tLes quatre vaccins de Pasteur --tDe la sérothérapie aux anatoxines --tLes vaccins contre le choléra et la peste --tDes germes entiers à L'ARN messager --tRéflexions --tLes liens incestueux entre scientifiques et la presse scientifique --tLes scientifiques face aux fake news --tDes savants d'antan aux chercheurs d'aujourd'hui --tLa course à la connaissance --tIndex des noms cités.8 aJean-Marc Cavaillon nous retrace l'histoire de l'humanité confrontée aux pandémies, et la contribution de quelques savants célèbres et de beaucoup d'autres injustement oubliés qui identifièrent les miasmes, les animalcules, les virus, les germes responsables de tant de maux. Il relate leurs efforts pour lutter contre les infections, proposer l'hygiène, offrir les traitements antiseptiques ou antibiotiques, et prévenir les maladies infectieuses à l'aide des vaccins. Il met en parallèle de surprenantes analogies entre des évènements historiques et des évènements associés à la pandémie de COVID-19, devenue le fil rouge de ce récit: les liens incestueux entre certains scientifiques et la presse scientifique, les querelles entre doctes docteurs, entre contagionnistes et anticontagionnistes, entre rassuristes et alarmistes. Il rappelle l'usage des masques initié au XVIIe siècle, l'extraordinaire saga de la vaccination accompagnée de la concomitante réticence face aux vaccins. Autant d'évènements témoins de la guerre déclarée aux microbes et de la guerre des égos. Sur son chemin, il croise ses héros favoris, Metchnikoff et Semmelweis, déniche des génies oubliés, et n'hésite pas à égratigner l'image d'Épinal de Louis Pasteur, entretenue par ses hagiographes.12aCommunicable Diseasesxhistory22aVaccinesxhistory22aEpidemicsxhistory22aCommunicable Disease Controlxhistory  aAUTH01554cas a2200481 a 101148145DNLM20251126101949.0cr|cn ||||||||020430c20039999nyuqr p       0   a0eng    a  20022135420 a1539-8285l1539-828521  a(OCoLC)49694335  aNSDcNSDdNLMdSBHdDLCdNSDdDNLM  alcansdpanlmcopyc  9United States00aRA773.6b.H4300aW1bHE299MW00a025.06/362122010aJ Consum Health Internet2dnlm0 aJ. consum. health Internet 0aJournal of consumer health on the Internetb(Print)00aJournal of consumer health on the Internet.30aConsumer health on the Internet30aHealth on the Internet  aBinghamton, NY :bHaworth Press,cc2003-  av. :bill. ;c22 cm.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 7, no. 1 (2003)-  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 7, no. 2 (2003).0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online.12aComputer Communication Networks22aCommunity Participation22aDelivery of Health Care 2aPeriodical0 x1539-829300tHealth care on the Internetx1089-4187w(DLC)   97641973w(OCoLC)349913694 uhttps://www.tandfonline.com/loi/wchi20  aAUTH02403nam a2200421 i 9918986638106676DNLM20251124140617.0230510t20242024nyua     b    001 0 eng    a  2023008361  a9781032039190qhardcover  a1032039191qhardcover  a9781032039183qpaperback  a1032039183qpaperback  z9781003189701qelectronic book  a(OCoLC)1380997731  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCFdOCLCOdIG#dYDXdOCLCOdOCLCL  apcc  9United States00aRJ505.G7bS527 202400aWS 350.5500a618.92/89152223/eng/202306011 aSheppard, Tony L.,eauthor.10aGroup psychotherapy with children :bcore principles for effective practice /cTony L. Sheppard and Zachary J. Thieneman. 1aNew York :bRoutledge, Taylor & Francis Group,c2024. 4c©2024  a191 pages :billustrations ;c26 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aAGPA group therapy training and practice series  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  a"This book guides the reader through the process of creating evidence-based therapy groups for children. Introducing an interpersonal theoretical framework that maximizes the interactional and experiential learning and growth components of groups with children, this curriculum offers the child group therapist a theoretical foundation that gives structure to existing techniques and an approach that is multiculturally sensitive and grounded in brain science. A deeper understanding of the mechanisms of change that operate in children's groups is central to the theme, including an emphasis on play and "learning by doing" through real-life clinical examples which permit readers of all levels to achieve a better understanding of how child groups function. Readers of this book will come away with a deeper understanding of the "power cell" of group therapy: working interpersonally in the here and now, specifically with children"--cProvided by publisher.12aPsychotherapy, Groupxmethods22aChild1 aThieneman, Zachary J.,eauthor. 0aAGPA group therapy training and practice series  aAUTH01248pam a2200385 i 9918991788106676DNLM20251120094440.0230220s2023    sz a     b    001 0 eng    aGBC3451052bnb  a9783031249297qhardback  a3031249291qhardback  z9783031249303qebook  a(OCoLC)1371842009  aUKMGBbengerdacUKMGBdOCLCFdOCLCOdOCLCLdOHX  apcc  9Switzerland00aWL 35404a616.822300aNeurobiological and psychological aspects of brain recovery /cLaura Petrosini, editor.  aSecond edition. 1aCham :bSpringer,c[2023]  axxiv, 406 pages :billustrations (some colour) ;c24 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aContemporary clinical neuroscience  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.12aBrain Injuriesxtherapy22aCognitive Reserve22aNeurological Rehabilitation22aRecovery of Function1 aPetrosini, Laura,eeditor. 0aContemporary clinical neuroscience.  aAUTH01994cas a2200481   7807112DNLM20251126113745.0cr|cn#||||||||780907d19772018gw || p       0    0ger    a0342-3026l0342-3026  aLABOD3  a(DNLM)L00660000(s)z(DNLM)L00655900(s)  a(OCoLC)04454370  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 ageraeng  9Germany00aW1bLA2055D00aLaboratoriumsmedizin.13aLaboratoriums Med