y, ethnopharmacology, natural products, and molecular pathways /cChristophe Wiart.30aMedicinal plants of the world for aging  aFirst edition. 1aBoca Raton, FL :bCRC Press,c2024. 4c©2024  axv, 294 pages :billustrations ;c25 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and indexes.  a"Handbook of Medicinal Plants of the World for Aging: Botany, Ethnopharmacology, Natural products, and Molecular Pathways provides an unprecedented comprehensive overview of more than 100 plants used globally as medicine with the potential to prevent premature ageing. This handbook covers the pathophysiology of ageing from the molecular and cellular to organs levels, as well as the current state of knowledge about the mode of action of natural products from plants onto the pathophysiological pathways related to: (i) cardiovascular system and metabolism, (ii) central nervous system, (iii) kidneys, (iv) bones, (v) skin and hair, and (vi) immune system"--cProvided by publisher.12aPlants, Medicinal 2aHandbook  aAUTH01102cas a2200385 a 9424940DNLM20251126101622.0cr|cn#||||||||960815c19uu9999it tr p       0||| 0ita    asn 93026094   a0391-2868l0391-2868y0391-2668  aTEFADJ  a(DNLM)SR0051585(s)  a(OCoLC)27868483  aFUcFUdDNLM  9Italy00aW1bTE5160 aTerapia familiare (Rome, Italy)10aTerapia familiare :brivista interdisciplinare di ricerca ed intervento relazionale.  aRoma :bI.T.F.,3 aRoma :bI. T. F  av.  aThree no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aDescription based on: N. 8 (dic. 1980); title from cover.  aAlso issued online 2aFamily Therapy 2aPeriodical2 aI.T.F. (Organization)0 x1972-54424 uhttp://digital.casalini.it/19725442  aAUTH01226cam a2200313 i 450000100100000000300050001000500170001500800410003203500200007304000350009304400180012806000200014611000600016624500630022624600480028926400510033730000220038833600260041033700280043633800270046450000220049154001420051358300390065558300720069465000530076665000660081965100180088599900090090360620250RDNLM20251120135841.0820514s1906    mau           000 0 eng    a(OCoLC)14776064  aDNLMbengerdad20251120dDNLM  9United States00aHVbM4085r 19061 aMassachusetts.bCommission on the Adult Blind,eauthor.10aReport of the Massachusetts Commission on the Adult Blind.1 aReport of the Commission on the Adult Blind 1aBoston :bWright & Potter Printing Co.,c1906.  a32 pages ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aTitle from cover.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202011192pda5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20251120lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM12aPersons with Visual Disabilitiesxrehabilitation22aPersons with Visual Disabilitiesxstatistics & numerical data 2aMassachusetts  aAUTH04571nam a2200409 i 9918986637706676DNLM20251113104200.0231006t20242024enka     b    001 0 eng    a  2023939915  a1401906970  a1529733030q(paperback)  a9781529733037q(paperback)  a1529733049q(hardback)  a9781529733044q(hardback)  a(OCoLC)1401905710z(OCoLC)1401906970  aYDXbengerdacYDXdBDXdOCLCQdOCLCLdOC3dYT1dYDXdS2HdOCLCQdUKRCNdOCLCOdY@YdCQC  apcc  9England 4aRC440b.E87 202400aWY 16004a616.89/0231qOCoLC223/eng/2023112000aEssentials of mental health nursing /cedited by Karen M. Wright and Mick McKeown.  a2nd edition. 1aLondon :bSage,c[2024] 4c©2024  axxvi, 858 pages:billustrations ;c26 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references (page 836) and index.0 aThe context and nature of mental health care in the twenty-first century  -- Overview of mental health nurse education and training -- Working with other professionals -- Meaningful service user involvement -- Working with families and carers -- Championing equalities and addressing vulnerability in mental health care -- Organisations and settings for mental health care -- The policy context for contemporary mental health care -- Madness and the law Independent advocacy in mental health care -- The ethical mental health nurse -- Sociological understandings of mental health -- Critical psychological ideas and practices Philosophical understanding of mental health -- A service user perspective Psychiatric understandings of mental health -- Spiritual care: understanding service users, understanding ourselves -- Public mental health: prevention and promotion -- Psychopharmacology for mental health nurses -- Wellbeing in mental health care -- Recovery-orientated practice -- Employment and recovery in mental health care -- Compassionate communication in mental health care -- Meeting the physical health needs of mental health service users -- Therapeutic engagement for mental health care Mental health assessment -- Care planning Mental health care coordination -- Mental health risk assessment: a personalised approach -- Minimising violence and related harms -- Cognitive behavioural therapies -- Psychosocial interventions to support carers -- Self-help and peer support in recovery -- Therapeutic communities, democracy and the new recovery movement dementia: assessment and care approaches -- Care of people experiencing eating disorders -- Children and young people’s mental health care -- Non-medical alternatives for crisis care -- Primary mental health care -- Palliative and end-of-life care in mental health care -- Working compassionately with people who self-harm -- Democratic leadership for mental health care -- Clinical supervision in mental health nursing Transferable skills and transition: becoming a mental health nurse and beyond -- Commissioning for mental health services -- Compassionate mental health care in times of uncertainty.  a"Are you studying mental health nursing and want a book that covers all you need to know?  Look no further. As it says in the name, this is an essential text for students. Split into 5 parts, this book delves into the context of mental health, key concepts and debates, skills for care and therapeutic approaches, tailoring care to people with specific needs, and transition to practice.   Updated to include more content from those with lived experience, this new edition also includes: - Voices of mental health service users and practitioners, giving you a real insight in the field - Critical thinking stop points and debates, allowing you to develop your wider skills and knowledge - Case studies to bring the content to life - Chapter summaries, so you know what the main takeaways are for each chapter - Further reading and useful websites, allowing you to do your own research  The editors, Karen M. Wright and Mick McKeown come with a wealth of experience in mental health nursing. The variety of contributors also reflect different experiences in different contexts." --cProvided by publisher.12aPsychiatric Nursing1 aWright, Karen M.,eauthor.1 aMcKeown, Mick,eeditor.  aAUTH01432cas a2200469 a 8804264DNLM20251126100047.0cr|cn#||||||||880407c19889999nyuqr p       0    0eng    a   88646970 zsn 87007656  a0896-4289l0896-4289  aBEMEEF  a(DNLM)SR0062060(s)  a(OCoLC)17153135  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1bBE13GK0 aBehavioral medicine (Washington, D.C.)10aBehav Med2dnlm 0aBehavioral medicineb(Washington, D.C.)10aBehavioral medicine.  a[Washington, DC] :bHeldref Publications,c[c1988-3 32010- :aNew York :bRoutledge  av. :bill.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 14, no. 1 (spring 1988)-  aTitle from cover.1 aMEDLINEbv14n1,spring 1988-0 aPubMedbv14n1,spring 1988-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso