ion (in English) of the titles; typewritten title-pages dated 1922 with "Robert E. Noble, M.D./Librarian" at bottom; typewritten note inserted between title pages, "Gen. Noble: It is with Mr. Dundas help I am able to make this translation. If Mr. Neumann could supply the authors, titles and translations, of the incunabs he has - the Library would have a complete list of its Incunabs with translations - It would be very interesting to those who are not scholars. M.D.S.".5DNLM  aCopy 4 interleaved with typewritten translation (in English) of the titles; typewritten title-pages dated 1922 with "Robert E. Noble, M.D./Librarian" at bottom, crossed out in ink with "CC McCulloch" written above; inscription on interleaving page between title pages, "This volume received from Washington May 3, 1945. Courtesy Mr. Austin [?] Cleveland Branch. See letter from Mr. Dundas in AMA 324."5DNLM  aCopy 5, "Miss Spiers" written in ink on the front cover; annotations in pencil and pen throughout.5DNLM  aAlso available online.  aCondition reviewedc20130211lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM1 adigitized.c20132pda5DNLM22aLibrary of the Surgeon-General's Office (U.S.)12aIncunabula as Topic 2aBibliography0 aAnnals of medical history.4 uhttp://resource.nlm.nih.gov/57610600R  aAUTH01330cas a2200421   0076033DNLM20251113105126.0cr|cn#||||||||670405c19669999sz  x         0    0eng    a   67004882 z86027674z89024452z98012266z99037076z00037076z2003047736z2004013518z2004024871  a0079-6492l0079-6492  aPRNSBW  a(DNLM)P48200000(s)  a(OCoLC)01624451  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Switzerland00aW1bPR67310aProg Neurol Surg2dnlm00aProgress in neurological surgery.  aChicago :bYear Book Medical Publishers,c1966-3 3<1987-> :aBasel :bKarger  av.billus.  aIrrregular  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av. 1-       1966-  aEditor: 1966- H. Krayenbühl [et al.]1 aMEDLINEbv19, 2006-v35, 2