Med2dnlm00aAmerican journal of law & medicine.3 aAmerican journal of law and medicine  aBoston :bAmerican Society of Law & Medicine3132021- :a[Cambridge] :bCambridge University Press  av.billus.,ports.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 av.1-    Mar. 1975-1 aMEDLINEbv1n1,Mar. 1975-1 aPubMedbv1n1,Mar. 1975-1 aIndex medicus  aAlso issued online.  3Vol. 13, no. 1 (1987)c19890912fNotice not publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper 2aJurisprudence 2aMedicine 2aPeriodical2 aAmerican Society of Law and Medicine.0 x2375-835X4 uhttps://journals.sagepub.com/home/jlm4 uhttps://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/american-journal-of-law-and-medicine  aAUTH00714cam a22002291  45000010009000000030005000090050017000140080041000310350020000720400021000920440010001130600023001231000037001462450020001832600020002033000015002233360026002383370028002643380027002925010156003199990009004752721789RDNLM20251113150747.0841201s1750    it            000|0 ita    a(OCoLC)14334990  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Italy00aWZ 260bP278c 17501 aPascoli, Alessandro,d1669-1757.13aIl corpo-umano.  aVenezia,c1750.  a255, 52 p.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aNLM copy, bound with: Marcelli Malpighii, et Jo. Mariae Lancisii Consultationum medicarum nonnullarumque dissertationum collectio Venetiis, 1747.5DNLM  aAUTH03230pam a2200397 i 9918986643406676DNLM20251114102302.0221108s2023    enka     b    001 0 eng    a  2022052375  a9781800621831q(paperback)  a1800621833q(paperback)  z9781800621848q(ebook)  z9781800621855q(epub)  a(OCoLC)1350966392  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCFdBDXdYDXdOCLCOdICKdIG#  apcc  9England00aRA781b.B46 202300aQT 25600a613.7223/eng/202211171 aBethell, Hugh,eauthor.10aExercise :ba scientific and clinical overview /cDr Hugh J.N. Bethell and Professor David Brodie. 1aWallingford, Oxfordshire, UK ;aBoston, MA, USA :bCABI,c[2023] 4c©2023  axii, 180 pages :billustrations ;c25 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.0 aSection one : the background to exercise -- A brief historical context for exercise -- The muscles and types of exercise -- Oxygen as the fuel of aerobic exercise -- Section two: quantifying exercise -- Exercise dose -- Physical fitness : the best measure of exercise capacity -- The components of overall exercise volume -- Population activity levels -- How fit is the general population? -- Evidence : interpreting the science -- Section three : exercise, fitness and disease -- Obesity -- High blood pressure -- Dyslipidaemia -- Diabetes -- The metabolic syndrome -- Coronary Heart Disease (CHD) -- Peripheral vascular disease -- Stroke -- Parkinson's disease -- Psychological ill health -- Dementia and cognition -- Lung disease -- Cancer -- Osteoporosis -- Other conditions -- Section four : other issues with exercise -- Frailty -- Longevity -- Social and economic cost of inactivity -- Encouraging exercise -- Sedentary behavior -- Complications of exercise -- Excuses to avoid exercise -- Conclusions.  a"This book is about exercise -- what it is, how it affects the individual, how it is measured and most of all what benefits it brings. Beginning with an introduction to the history and biology of exercise, the authors review the interactions between exercise and specific diseases, such as diabetes, coronary heart disease, cancer and many more, before considering exercise in a wider health context. The book covers: Current societal norms, as well as the social and economic costs of inactivity. Exercise for life -- from starting young, to pregnancy, longevity and frailty. Complications of exercise. The intersections of behavioural psychology and exercise, such as encouragement and excuse making. With comprehensive and clear explanations based on sound science, yet written in an approachable and accessible style, this book is a valuable resource for students of medicine, public health, physiotherapy, sports science, coaching and training." -- Back cover.12aExercisexphysiology22aPhysical Fitness1 aBrodie, David A.,d1946-eauthor.  aAUTH01472nam a2200337 i 101777273DNLM20251119145749.0210317r18801880miu           000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5513 no.51 aAllen, John K.,dactive 19th century,eauthor.10aAir-moistening /cread by Jno. K. Allen, of Lansing, at the Sanitary Convention in Grand Rapids, Mich., February 18, 1880, and illustrated with samples of the air-moistener manufactured by I.W. Parmenter. 1a[Lansing] :b[publisher not identified],c[1880]  a1 folded sheet (3 pages) ;c23 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  asheetbnb2rdacarrier  aCaption title.  a"Reprinted from the Annual report of the Michigan State Board of Health for the year 1880."  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202504075DNLM12aAir22aHeatingxinstrumentation22aVentilationxinstrumentation 2aAddress1 aSanitary Conventionn(2nd :d1880 :cGrand Rapids, Mich.)0 aAnnual report of the Michigan State Board of Health.  aAUTH01065pam a2200361 i 9918863387706676DNLM20251118131012.0240302s2024    gw a          001 0 ger    a9783110660111qhardbound  a3110660113qhardbound  z9783110663051qPDF  z9783110660319qEPUB  a(OCoLC)1424848755  aOHXbengerdacOHXdOCLCQ  apcc  9Germany00aWP 140 7aRG2lcco04a616.9qOCoLC1 aMylonas, Ioannis,d1974-eauthor.10aPraxis der gynäkologischen Infektiologie /cIoannis Mylonas. 1aBerlin :bDe Gruyter,c[2024] 4c©2024  axiv, 582 pages :bcolor illustrations ;c25 cm  atext