s -- Computer Science and the Foundation of Knowledge Model -- Introduction to Cognitive Science and Cognitive Informatics -- Ethical Applications of Informatics -- History and Evolution of Nursing Informatics -- Nursing Informatics as a Specialty -- Legislative Aspects of Nursing Informatics: HIPAA, HITECH, and Beyond -- Systems Development Life Cycle: Nursing Informatics and Organizational Decision-Making -- Administrative Information Systems -- The Human-Technology Interface -- Electronic Security -- Achieving Excellence by Managing Workflow and Initiating Quality Projects -- The Electronic Health Record and Clinical Informatics -- Informatics Tools to Promote Patient Safety, Quality -- Outcomes, and Interdisciplinary Collaboration -- Patient Engagement and Connected Health -- Using Informatics to Promote Community and Population Health -- Telenursing and Remote Access Telehealth -- Nursing Informatics and Nursing Education -- Simulation, Game Mechanics, Virtual Worlds, and Realities in Nursing Education -- Nursing Research: Data Collection, Processing, and Analysis -- Informatics Based Research Processes: Data Mining and Artificial Intelligence -- Generating and Translating Evidence for Practice -- The Art of Caring in Technology-Laden Environments -- Our Expanding Realities and the Metaverse.  a"Nursing Informatics and the Foundation of Knowledge is a foundational text designed to teach nursing students the core concepts of knowledge management while demystifying nursing informatics, a complex and ever-evolving specialty area. A practical guide for understanding how to leverage modern technology in order to provide safe and high-quality patient care, this text shows students how to acquire, process and disseminate knowledge"--cProvided by publisher.12aNursing Informatics22aKnowledge22aKnowledge Management22aNursing Research1 aMastrian, Kathleen Garver,eauthor,eeditor.  aCIP01755cas a22004817i 9918988895806676DNLM20251125073400.0m     o  d        cr#|||||||||||190703c20149999mz || poo    f0    0por    y2311-3308  a(OCoLC)1552758116  aDNLMbengerdad20251124cDNLMdDNLM0 aporbeng  af-mz---  9Mozambique 4aR98.5.P7bR4800aW110aRev Mocamb Cienc Saude2dnlm00aRevista Moçambicana de ciências de saúde.30aCiências de saúde1 aRMCS 1a[Maputo] :bInstituto Nacional da Saúde, Ministério da Saúde,c[2014]-  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Volume 1, número 1 (março 2014).0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aNo volume issued for 2017.  aAlso issued in print.  aPortuguese with abstracts in English and Portuguese  a"Publicação oficial do Instituto Nacional de Saúde de Moçambique"--Page 2 of cover, março 2014  aDescription based on: Volume 1, número 1 (março 2014); publisher's website (viewed November 13, 2025).  aLatest issue consulted: Volume 10, número 01 (abril 2024) (viewed November 13, 2025).12aPublic Health22aMedicine 2aMozambique 2aPeriodical2 aInstituto Nacional da Saúde (Mozambique),eissuing body.40uhttps://ins.gov.mz/publicacoes/revista-cientifica-rmcs/  aAUTH04368cam a2200433 i 9918986643706676DNLM20251113152003.0221006t20232023paua     b    001 0 eng    aGBC2I06882bnb  a9781975176983q(hardcover)  a1975176987q(hardcover)  z9781975177003q(electronic publication)  a(OCoLC)1521297239  aUKMGBbengerdad20251113dOCLCFdTNFdYDXdAHMdOCLCOdIBIdDNLM  apcc  9United States 4aRG527.5.U48bD46 202300aWP 14104a61822300aDiagnostic medical sonography.pObstetrics and gynecology /c[edited by] Susan Raatz Stephenson, Julia Dmitrieva.  aFifth edition. 1aPhiladelphia :bWolters Kluwer,c[2023] 4c©2023  axiii, 910 pages :billustrations ;c29 cm  atext2rdacontent  aunmediated2rdamedia  avolume2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.00tOrientation and labeling in obstetric and gynecologic imaging --tSonographic image optimization --tPrinciples of scanning technique in gynecologic ultrasound --tObstetric scanning primer --tFoundational ultrasound ergonomics for obstetrics and gynecology --tEmbryonic development of the female genital system --tCongenital anomalies of the female genital --tThe female cycle --tNormal anatomy of the female pelvis --tDoppler evaluation of the pelvis --tPediatric pelvis --tBenign disease of the female pelvis --tMalignant disease of the uterus and cervix --tMalignant diseases of the ovary --tPelvic inflammatory disease and endometriosis --tImaging the intrauterine device --tThe use of ultrasound in the first trimester --tSonographic evaluation of first-trimester complications --tSonographic assessment of the ectopic pregnancy --tAssessment of fetal age and size in the second and third trimester --tNormal placenta and umbilical cord --tAbnormalities of the placenta and umbilical cord --tSonographic assessment of the fetal head --tSonographic assessment of the fetal neck and spine --tFetal echocardiography --tSonographic assessment of the fetal chest --tSonographic assessment of the fetal abdomen (includes abdominal wall) --tSonographic assessment of the fetal genitourinary system and fetal pelvis --tNormal and abnormal fetal limbs --tThe biophysical profile --tMultiple gestations --tFetal growth restriction --tPatterns of fetal anomalies --tEffects of maternal disease on pregnancy --tThe postpartum uterus --tInterventional ultrasound --tAssisted reproducitve technologies --tComplementary imaging of the female reproductive system --t3D and 4D imaging in obstetrics and gynecology.  a"Part of the highly regarded Diagnostic Medical Sonography series, Susan Raatz Stephenson and Julia Dmitrieva's Obstetrics and Gynecology, 5th Edition, thoroughly covers the core content students need to master in today's rigorous sonography programs. Careful, collaborative editing ensures consistency across all three titles in this series: The Vascular System, Abdomen and Superficial Structures, and Obstetrics and Gynecology, providing the right content at the right level for both students and instructors. Diagnostic Medical Sonography: Obstetrics and Gynecology, 5th Edition, is now available with Lippincott® Connect! Lippincott® Connect enables you to personalize your teaching and enhance your students' course experience in a customizable, all-in-one learning solution combining assessment, multimedia content, and an interactive eBook. Instructors can create assignments, assess students' knowledge, and track their progress. Students maximize efficiency through valuable feedback and remediation. Key performance insights are reported in a user-friendly dashboard that allows instructors and students to tailor their teaching and learning experiences." --cProvided by publisher.12aGenital Diseases, Femalexdiagnostic imaging12aUltrasonography22aFetal Diseasesxdiagnostic imaging22aPregnancy Complicationsxdiagnostic imaging22aUltrasonography, Prenatal1 aStephenson, Susan Raatz,eeditor.1 aDmitrieva, Julia,eeditor.  aAUTH02663nam a2200385 i 9918992896106676DNLM20251113085508.0240405s2024    sz a     b    001 0 eng    a9783031598142  a3031598148  a9783031598159qebook  a(OCoLC)1428700706  aYDXbengerdacYDXdBDX  apcc  9Switzerland00aW1bAD559 v.1448 202410aQZ 15000aCytokine storm syndrome /cRandy Q. Cron, Edward M. Behrens, editors.  aSecond edition. 1aCham, Switzerland :bSpringer,c[2024]  axvi, 628 pages :billustrations ;c26 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aAdvances in Experimental Medicine and Biology,x0065-25989 ;vvolume 1448  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  aCytokine Storm Syndromes, including HLH and MAS, are frequently fatal disorders, particularly if not recognized early and treated during presentation. The genetics of Cytokine Storm Syndromes are being defined with many of the risk alleles giving rise to mutations in the perforin-mediated cytolytic pathway used by CD8 cytotoxic T cells and natural killer cells. These are being studied using murine models. Up to 10% of the general population may carry risk alleles for developing Cytokine Storm Syndromes, and Cytokine Storm Syndromes are being increasingly recognized around the world in pediatric and adult hospitals. A variety of infectious, rheumatic, and oncologic triggers are commonly associated with Cytokine Storm Syndromes, but understanding this disorder is critical for all researchers and physicians to ensure timely and appropriate therapy. This second edition addresses all aspects of the disorder, from genetics, pathophysiology, and ongoing research, to clinical presentations, risk factors and treatment. New-to-this-edition features include dedicated chapters on severe COVID-19 CSS, and post-COVID CSS of multi-system inflammatory syndrome in children (MIS-C). In addition, novel topics including CSS associated with Castleman disease, pregnancy, therapeutics, transplantation, and cardiac bypass, as well as treatment with JAK inhibitors are addressed.12aCytokine Release Syndrome22aLymphohistiocytosis, Hemophagocytic22aMacrophage Activation Syndrome1 aCron, Randy Q.,d1963-eeditor1 aBehrens, Edward M.,eeditor. 0aAdvances in experimental medicine and biology ;vv.1448.x0065-25989  aAUTH01151nam a2200349 i 9918977461706676DNLM20251117080059.0241019t20242024gw a     b    001 0 ger    a9783662644034q(paperback)  z9783662644041q(eBook)  a(OCoLC)1462362616  aOHXbengerdacOHX  apcc  9Germany00aWO 178 7aRD2lcco00aPerioperative Medizin für die Allgemein- und Viszeralchirurgen /cJohanna C. Wagner, Christoph-Thomas Germer, Armin Wiegering (Hrsg.). 1aBerlin, Germany :bSpringer,c[2024] 4c©2024  axv, 384 pages :billustrations ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avo