cardiography --tCardiac catheterisation --tRadiological imaging --tCardiopulmonary bypass --tCardiopulmonary bypass scenarios --tAdjuncts to cardiopulmonary bypass --tMyocardial protection --tAortic valve disease --tMitral valve disease --tTricuspid valve disease --tInfective endocarditis --tThoracic aortic disease --tCoronary artery disease --tHeart failure --tArrhythmia surgery --tPericardial disease, cardiac tumours and cardiac trauma --tPulmonary embolism --tCardiac anaesthesia and intensive care management --tPostoperative management --tStatistics --gAppendix I:tTransoesophageal echocardiographic views --gAppendix II:tTransthoracic echocardiographic views --gAppendix III:tNormal echocardiographic values --gAppendix IV:tStandard coronary angiographic views --gAppendix V:tNormal arterial blood gas values --gAppendix VI:tNormal cardiac physiological values --gAppendix VII:tAHA guidelines for quantifying the severity of valvular disease --gAppendix VIII:tStages of valvular heart disease.  aKey Questions in Cardiac Surgery provides a systematic overview of the important topics in contemporary adult cardiac surgical practice. The text is evidence-based, incorporating current literature and has been updated from the 1st edition with the most recent American Heart Association and European Society of Cardiology guidelines. This illustrated concise text is a practical and clinically focused book that covers all the key questions in cardiac surgery. Additional chapters on statistics and pulmonary embolism have been included, with the main chapters having been updated describing contemporary surgical techniques and management philosophies. Whilst being an ideal reference for cardiac surgical trainees and residents, especially when undertaking their cardiothoracic surgery board examinations, this book is also of great value to other specialties involved in the care of cardiac surgical patients, including cardiologists, cardiothoracic intensivists, nurses and physiotherapists.12aCardiac Surgical Procedures12aCardiovascular Diseasesxsurgery22aThoracic Surgery1 aViola, Nicola,eauthor.1 aOhri, Sunil K.,eauthor.  aAUTH01745cas a2200493 a 101219148DNLM20251126082757.0cr|cn#||||||||040602c20059999sz  x p       0    0fre    a  2005243628  a1660-9379l1660-9379  a(OCoLC)60388257  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 afrebeng  alcd  9Switzerland00aW1bRE93F10aRev Med Suisse2dnlm00aRevue médicale suisse.  aGenève :bMédecine et Hygiène,c2005-  av. :bill.  aWeekly (46 issues per year)  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (5 janv. 2005)-  aTitle from cover.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 1, no. 3 (19 janv. 2005).1 aMEDLINEbv1n1, Jan. 5 2005-1 aPubMedbv1n1, Jan. 5 2005-  aAlso issued online.  aArticles in French; summaries also in English.  aRevue officielle de la Société médicale de la Suisse romande et de la Société suisse de médecine interne.  aMerger of: Revue médicale de la Suisse romande, and: Médecine et hygiène.12aMedicine 2aPeriodical2 aSociété médicale de la Suisse romande.2 aSchweizerische Gesellschaft für Innere Medizin.0 x3042-678214tRevue médicale de la Suisse romandex0035-3655w(DLC)sn 86012853w(OCoLC)176421614tMédecine et hygiènex0025-6749w(DLC)sn 85005766w(OCoLC)062688604 uhttp://www.revmed.ch  aAUTH01025nam a2200325 i 9918785283706676DNLM20251113102054.0231127s2022    cc a     b    001 0 chi    a9787030736857  a20230302-27  aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  apcc  9China00aQT 371 aZhou, Changren,d1956-eauthor.10aHai yang sheng wu cai liao /cZhou Changren deng zhu.1 aMarine biomaterials  aDi 1 ban. 1aBeijing :bKe xue chu ban she,c2022 nian 12 yue.  axi, 321 pages :billlustrations ;c24 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aSheng wu cai liao ke xue yu gong cheng cong shu  aIncludes bibliographical reference and index.12aBiocompatible Materials22aMarine Biologyxmethods 0aSheng wu cai liao ke xue yu gong cheng cong shu  aAUTH01510nam a2200361 i 9918299688106676DNLM20251120135738.0211108r18781878nyu     r     000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5561 no.91 aPallen, Montrose A.q(Montrose Anderson),d1836-eauthor.10aKolpo-cystotomy10aKolpo-cystotomy, or, Artificial vesico-vaginal fistula /cby Montrose A. Pallen.1 aArtificial vesico-vaginal fistula 1aNew York :bWilliam Wood & Co.,c1878.  a11 pages ;c23 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  a"Reprinted from the American journal of obstetrics and diseases of women and children, vol. XI, no. II, April, 1878."  a"Read before the New York Obstetrical Society, Dec. 18th, 1877."--Page 3, footnote.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202504075DNLM12aCystotomy22aCystitisxsurgery22aVesicovaginal Fistulaxsurgery 2aCase Reports2 aNew York Obstetrical Society.0 aAmerican journal of obstetrics and diseases of women and children.  aAUTH02126nam a2200373 a 9918917724406676DNLM20251118111527.0220822t20222022fr     f d    001 0cfre    a9782140253867 (pbk.)  a2140253868 (pbk.)  a(OCoLC)1341651811  aLGGbengcLGGdLGGdERASPdOCLCFdOCLCOdOCLCQ  9France 4aRC666.5b.M33 202200aWG 11.104a610.91 aMaarek, Martine.10aHistoire de la cardiologie à travers ses noms propres :bdictionnaire historique des termes éponymes en cardiologie /cMartine Maarek ; préface de Jean-Noël Fabiani-Salmon. 1aParis :bHarmattan,c[2022] . 4c© 2022  a325, [3] pages ;c24 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aActeurs de la sciences  aIncludes indexes.  aEn regardant évoluer des voiliers, poussés par le vent, le cardiologue Jeremy Swan eut l'idée de concevoir un cathéter souple guidé par un ballonnet gonflable et mû par le courant sanguin, la « sonde de Swan-Ganz », qui révolutionna la prise en charge des patients en unités de soins intensifs. En observant des enfants s'amuser à communiquer à distance, de part et d'autre d'une longue poutre, René Laennec inventa le « stéthoscope », permettant l'auscultation « médiate ».À la suite d'une erreur de manipulation, fut réalisée la première coronarographie par Frank Mason Sones. Ainsi, la « technique de Sones » se répandit partout dans le monde. L'auteur raconte, par le biais des noms propres accordés à des maladies, des termes anatomiques, des procédures chirurgicales, l'histoire des découvertes et des inventions qui ont permis à des médecins de graver leur nom sur l'autel de la cardiologie.12aCardiologyxhistory22aCardiologistsxhistory 2aDictionary 2aBiography 0aActeurs de la science.x625-3302  aAUTH01403nam a2200349 i 9918225878006676DNLM20251125075136.0940707r18741873pau           000 0 eng    a(OCoLC)54151823  aYUSbengcYUSdOCLCGdPHAdTEUdOCLCFdOCLCOdOCLCQerdadDNLM  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5576 no.271 aRuschenberger, W. S. W.q(William Samuel Waithman),d1807-1895,eauthor.10aOn the value of original scientific research /cby W.S.W. Ruschenberger. 1a[Philadelphia?] :b[publisher not identified],c[1874?]  a36 pages ;c24 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aCaption title.  a"Re-printed from the Penn monthly for November, 1873."  aAt head of title: Social Science Association of Philadelphia. Papers of 1874.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition revi