v6n1, Mar. 2015- ; selected citations only before this date0 aPMC  aAlso issued online.  aLatest issue consulted: Vol. 5, no. 1 (Mar. 2014).12aResearch Design22aMeta-Analysis as Topic 2aPeriodical2 aSociety for Research Synthesis Methodology.0 x1759-28874 uhttps://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/loi/175928874 uhttps://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/research-synthesis-methods4 uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=101543738  aAUTH02125nam a2200385 i 9918986572406676DNLM20251121152528.0240606s2024    enka     b    001 0 eng    a  2024441311  a1381546384  a9781839979088  a1839979089  a(OCoLC)1437893217z(OCoLC)1381546384  aLPUbengerdacLPUdOCLCOdYDXdIAXdOCLCOdDLCdOUPdIG#  apcc  9England 4aRA427.8b.A48 202400aWA 59004a6132231 aAltug, Ziya,eauthor.10aThe lifestyle medicine toolbox :bmind-body approaches for health promotion /cZ. Altug ; foreword by Dr. Melissa Sundermann. 1aLondon ;aPhiladelphia :bJessica Kingsley Publishers,c2024.  a366 pages :billustrations ;c25 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and indexes.  a"This holistic guide provides an integrative toolbox on how healthcare and fitness professionals can promote lifestyle medicine with their clients. Its clinical and evidence-informed approach focuses on the six primary lifestyle medicine factors: nutrition, exercise, sleep hygiene, stress management, risky substance use, and social connectedness. Each factor is enriched with strategies and advice, including anti-inflammatory recipes, self-guided visualisation, tips on how to break bad habits, sustainable fitness, and mind-body exercises. This book's nonpharmacological and nonsurgical focus allows clients to feel empowered in taking charge of their health through a plethora of resources and techniques. It provides clear, actionable steps and real-world examples in order to nurture sustainable changes that promote long-term health and healing"--Page [4] of cover.12aHealthy Lifestyle12aHealth Promotion22aMind-Body Therapiesxmethods22aHolistic Health1 aSundermann, Melissa,ewriter of foreword.  aAUTH00796cam a2200265   45000010008000000030005000080050017000130080041000300350020000710400021000910440010001120600023001222450094001452500013002392600050002523000022003023360026003243370028003503380027003785000026004056500014004316550017004458300059004629990009005210121246DNLM20251114073945.0671114s1952    cc ||||  |||| 00||0|chi    a(OCoLC)14546062  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9China00aWQ 165bC539c 195100aChu ji zhu chan xue /cZhong yang ren min zheng fu wei sheng bu fu you wei sheng ju bian.  aZai ban.  aTsinan]bHua dong yi wu sheng huo shec[1952]  a2, 110 p.billus.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aFirst published 1951. 2aMidwifery 2aPopular Work 0aFu you wei sheng chu ji jiao cai can kao zi liao ;v2.  aAUTH01256nam a2200385 i 9918986566606676DNLM20251117100211.0230812t20252025stka     b    001 0 eng    a9780323935494qpaperback  a0323935494qpaperback  a(OCoLC)1393205249  aYDXbengerdacYDXdBDXdOCLCOdOCLCQdOCLCLdYDXdOCLCOdOCLCQdYDX  apcc  9Scotland 4aRC815b.O23 202500aWU 140.804a617.6qOCoLC223/eng/202311201 aOdell, E. W.,eauthor.10aCawson's essentials of oral pathology and oral medicine /cEdward W. Odell.1 aEssentials of oral pathology and oral medicine1 aOral pathology and oral medicine  aTenth edition. 1a[Edinburgh?] :bElsevier,c[2025] 4c©2025  axi, 620 pages :billustrations (some color) ;c28 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.12aMouth Diseases22aSurgery, Oral22aDentistry, Operativexmethods22aTooth Diseases  aAUTH00967cas a22003494a 9886907DNLM20251113113258.0921124c19909999ii mr p       0||| 0eng   