25 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aSustainable development and biodiversity,x2352-474X ;vVolume 33  aIncludes bibliographical references.00gpart 1.tBiodiversity and endangered species of medicinal plants:g1.tThe current status of population extinction and biodiversity crisis of medicinal plants /rMihir Halder, Sumita Jha ;g2.tMedicinal plants and bioactive phytochemical diversity: a fountainhead of potential drugs against human diseases /rMihir Halder, Sumita Jha ;g3.tThreats and opportunities for sustainable use of medicinal plants in Brazilian Atlantic Forest based on the knowledge of indigenous peoples and local communities /rSofia Zank [and others] ;g4.tClimate change impact on medicinal plants: an insight from the IUCN red list of threatened species /rIyan Robiansyah [and others] ;g5.tSecuring conservation status of Paris polyphylla, a medicinally important plant of the Indian Himalayan region /rMohd Tariq, Shyamal Kumar Nandi, Indra Dutt Bhatt ;g6.tEndophytic fungal diversity in solanaceous medicinal plants and their beneficial impact /rDiptesh Biswas [and others] ;g7.tGenetic studies on threatened medicinal plants of Brazil: mind the gap! /rLiliana Essi ;g8.tMedicinal plants of North-East India: biodiversity and their ethnomedicinal values /rJudith Mary Lamo, Linu John, Satyawada Rama Rao --gpart 2.tConservation of medicinal plants:g9.tStrategies for conservation and sustainable use of medicinal plants /rMonika Sharma [and others] ;g10.tScientific databases for conservation of medicinal plants /rSyamsul Hidayat [and others] ;g11.tInternational trade of Medicinal and Aromatic Plants (MAPs) /rMarina Silalahi [and others] ;g12.tInventorization of ecology, ethnobotany, and conservation status of Dactylorhiza hatagirea: problems, progress, and prospects /rLaxman Singh [and others] ;g13.tConservation and sustainable use of medicinal plants /rMaura Lins dos Santos [and others] ;g14.tTraditional practices of ethnomedicinal plants in the north-eastern region of India and their conservation for sustainable utilization /rAsem Mipeshwaree Devi [and others] ;g15.tOccurrence and diversity of major Naphthoquinones in Higher Plants: their distribution and conservation strategies /rIndranil Santra [and others] ;g16.tAstragalus fridae: genetic source, applications, and conservation /rFardad Didaran [and others] ;g17.tTinospora cordifolia as a potential candidate for health care of post-menopausal women /rAnmol Bhandari, Gurcharan Kaur ;g18.tThe potential role of medicinal plants, traditional herbal medicines, and formulations to overcome SARS-CoV-2 induced health crisis /rMihir Halder, Rahul Bose, Sumita Jha ;g19.tBioactive compounds from medicinal plants and its therapeutic uses in the traditional healthcare system /rSubir Chandra Dasgupta --gpart 3.tConservation of medicinal plants by biotechnology:g20.tIn vitro conservation and propagation of endangered ethno-medicinal Orchids from the northeast region of India /rRoseeta Devi Mutum [and others] ;g21.tArtificial seed production and cryopreservation technology for conservation of plant germplasm with special reference to medicinal plants /rMonika Sharma, Prasann Kumar, Padmanabh Dwivedi ;g22.tBiotechnological studies on Nasturtium officinale (Watercress): an endangered species of significant relevance in medicine, cosmetic, and food industries /rMarta Klimek-Szczykutowicz, Halina Ekiert, Agnieszka Szopa ;g23.tIsatis tinctoria L. (Woad): cultivation, phytochemistry, pharmacology, biotechnology, and utilization /rNatalizia Miceli [and others] ;g24.tTissue culture techniques to conserve endangered medicinal plants with antimicrobial and antiviral activities /rSara Rahimi [and others] ;g25.tInsights into the in vitro approaches for the production of secondary metabolites towards the conservation of medicinal Orchids /rNutan Singh, Suman Kumaria ;g26.tBiotechnological approaches for ex situ conservation of medicinal plants /rAnrini Majumder, Dipasree Roychowdhury, Smita Ray ;g27.tConservation of medicinal plants by tissue culture techniques /rMansoureh Nazari, Mojtaba Kordrostami, Ali Akbar Ghasemi-Soloklui ;g28.tCurrent status of metabolic engineering of medicinal plants for production of plant-derived secondary metabolites /rMihir Halder, Shreyasi Roy ;g29.tStationary, agitated, and bioreactor cultures of Verbena officinalis L. (Common Vervain): a potential rich source of bioactive phenolic compounds for pharmacy, health food industry, and cosmetology /rPaweł Kubica [and others].  a"This contributed volume provides a comprehensive, in-depth and subject-based reviews on the current status of active ingredients, sustainable use, biodiversity and conservation of certain endangered medicinal plants. The book also explores conventional and non-conventional biotechnological interventions for their biodiversity conservation. Medicinal plants have been used in worldwide as a major source of raw material for the traditional herbal healthcare practices as well as for drug discovery and development in pharmaceutical industry. The cumulative consequences of various human activities and environmental factors cause decline in the biodiversity of medicinal plants at an unprecedented rate worldwide. Thus, the overall understanding of ecology, species and genetic diversity along with assessment of the status of different threats and their impact on medicinal plants is crucial to sustain existing biodiversity, its utilization and conservation. All the latest advancements in the biotechnological approaches for the conservation research of endangered medicinal plants and the future perspectives have been described. This book provides comprehensive reviews spreading over about 25 chapters divided in three sections. The chapters of this book are written by recognized scientists in their respective fields which are useful to students, academicians, researchers, botanists, biotechnologists, policy makers, conservationists and industries interested in biodiversity conservation and medicinal plant research for the production of secondary metabolites." --cProvided by publisher12aPlants, Medicinal12aBiodiversity12aConservation of Natural Resources1 aJha, Sumita,eeditor.1 aHalder, Mihir,eeditor. 0aSustainable development and biodiversity (Springer (Firm)) ;vv.33.  aAUTH02749nam a2200457 i 9918986637006676DNLM20251121101022.0230712t20242024moua     b    001 0 eng    aGBC2K41872bnb  a9780323761192q(paperback)  a0323761194q(paperback)  z9780323764971 (PDF ebook)  a(OCoLC)1390152683  aCQCbengerdacCQCdOCLCOdVRCdOCLCFdOCLCOdOCLCQdOCLCLdOCLCQdEBCdUNB  apcc  9United States00aWU 5004a344.730/413qOCoLC223/eng/20231120  aKF2910.D3bB44 20241 aMinihan-Anderson, Kristin,eauthor.10aEthics and law in dental hygiene /cKristin Minihan-Anderson.  aFourth edition. 1aSt. Louis, Missouri :bElsevier,c[2024] 4c©2024  axx, 184 pages :billustrations (chiefly color) ;c24 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aPreceded by Ethis and law in dental hygiene / Phyllis L. Beemsterboer. Third edition. [2017].  aIncludes bibliographical references (pages 169-173) and index.0 aSection I: ethics. Risk management -- Ethics and professionalism -- Ethical theory and philosophy -- Ethical principles and values -- Codes of ethics -- Ethical decision making in dental hygiene and dentistry -- Social responsibility -- Section II: law. Society and The State Dental Practice Act -- Dental hygienist-patient relationship -- Dental hygienist-dentist-employer relationship -- Section III: simulations and applications. Case studies, activities, and testlets.  a"Learn professional, practical ways to handle ethical and legal issues in dental practice! Ethics and Law in Dental Hygiene, 4th Edition provides a solid foundation in ethical theory and laws relating to oral healthcare professionals, including ethical conduct and social responsibility. An ethical decision-making model helps you unpack and analyze ethical dilemmas, and case scenarios challenge you to apply concepts to the real world. Written by a team of experts led by educator Kristin Minihan-Anderson, this book helps Dental Hygiene students prepare for the NBDHE exam and also serves as an valuable reference for practitioners looking to continue their professional growth." -- Publisher's website.12aEthics, Dental22aOral Hygienexethics22aLegislation, Dental22aProfessional-Patient Relations 2aUnited States 2aCase Reports1 aBeemsterboer, Phyllis.tEthics and law in dental hygiene.sThird edition.  aAUTH01372cas a22003737i 101293022DNLM20251120140110.0cr|cn#||||||||030707d20032010pl  x p       0    0pol    a1730-3524l1730-3524  a(OCoLC)82441770  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM0 apolbengfeng  9Poland00aW1bPR933C00aPrzegląd medyczny Uniwersytetu Rzeszowskiego.  aRzeszów :bWydawn. Uniwersytetu Rzeszowskiego  av. :bill.  aFour no. a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with T.1, z. 1 (2003); ceased T. 8, z. 2 (2010).zCf. ISSN Portal.  aDescription based on: T. 1, z. 3 (2003); title from cover.  aAlso issued online.  aText in Polish, summaries and table of contents also in English.12aMedicine 2aPeriodical2 aUniwersytet Rzeszowski.01tPrzegląd naukowy Instytutu Wychowania Fizycznego i Zdrowotnego Uniwersytetu Rzeszowskiegox1642-5936w(DLC)   2004210466w(OCoLC)5483095300tPrzegląd Medyczny Uniwersytetu Rzeszowskiego i Narodowego Instytutu Leków w Warszawiex2082-369X4 uhhttp://www.ejcem.ur.edu.pl/  aAUTH01183nam a2200337 i 9918957856906676DNLM20251121115427.0241216s2024    si a     b    000 0 eng    a9789819737048qhardbound  z9789819737055qebook  aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  apcc  9Singapo