oduction of Public Affairs Television, Inc.  a[New York, N.Y.] :bPublic Affairs Television,cc1990.  a1 videocassette (28 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  avideobv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier  aAt head of title: A World of ideas.  aFunding provided by the John D. and Catherine T. MacArthur Foundation and General Motors.  aClosed-captioned.0 aBill Moyers.8 a(Producer)  Jonas Salk is the developer of the polio vaccine and founder of the Salk Institute in La Jolla, California.  He talks about AIDS research and how the technique of "negotiating" with the AIDS virus offers a way of thinking about human beings as "part of, not apart from" nature.  Salk feels the development of an AIDS vaccine is just a matter of time and it is just a matter of strategy.  Solutions come through asking the right question, because the answer pre-exists.  It is the question that we have to define and discover.  You don't invent the answer, you reveal the answer.  aIssued also as a 3/4 in. videocassette.  aWill digitizec20210414xVHS to digital preservation filefNLM Policy for Fair Use of Copyrighted Materials2pda5DNLM12aSalk, Jonas,d1914-1995 2aAcquired Immunodeficiency Syndromexprevention & control 2aResearch 2aVaccines 2aInterview1 aSalk, Jonas,d1914-19951 aMoyers, Bill,d1934-2025.2 aWNET (Television station : New York, N.Y.)2 aWTTW (Television station : Chicago, Ill.)2 aWTVS-TV (Television station : Detroit, Mich.)2 aPublic Affairs Television (Firm)0 aWorld of ideas (Television program)  aHISRELb19991201  aAUTH01130nam a2200289 i 4500001001000000003000500010005001700015008004100032040003100073044001800104060003300122245014500155264006000300300002100360336002600381337002800407338002700435540014200462583003900604583004300643650001600686650001500702651001100717710006500728710003800793999000900831101777492DNLM20251128141506.0210323s1879    mau           000 0 eng   