t.  aRevised edition. 1aBoston :bD.C. Heath and Co.,c1909.  axi, 159 pages ;c20 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aHeath's modern language series  aIncludes index.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202011052pda5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20251120lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM12aPhilology, Romance22aLanguage Arts 0aHeath's modern language series.  aAUTH03100nam a2200457 i 9918986606106676DNLM20251125073354.0230927t20242024enka     b    001 0deng    a  2023041146  a1394894737  a9781032415376qhardcover  a1032415371qhardcover  a9781032415369qpaperback  a1032415363qpaperback  z9781003358572qelectronic book  a(OCoLC)1394895569z(OCoLC)1394894737  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdYDXdIG#  apcc  an-us---  9England00aRC554b.D39 202400aWM 460.200a616.89/14223/eng/202401251 aDaws, Loray,eauthor.10aJames F. Masterson :ba contemporary introduction /cLoray Daws. 1aAbingdon, Oxon ;aNew York, NY :bRoutledge, Taylor & Francis Group,c2024. 4c©2024  axii, 142 pages :billustrations ;c21 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aRoutledge introductions to contemporary psychoanalysis  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.0 aThe developmental self and object relations approach of James F Masterson MD -- Growing up, away, toward, or against- Masterson's Mahler -- Key concepts in the developmental self and object relations approach of James Masterson -- On psychological beginnings: Candace Orcutt's Mastersonian approach to the symbiotic experience -- Is there anybody out there? -- The tyranny of fusion and omnipotence -- the narcissistic dilemma -- Separation sensitivity and the borderline dilemma -- Conclusion and future of the Masterson approach.  a"In this volume, Loray Daws traces the life and work of Dr James F. Masterson, with a focus on the scientific development and later expansion of the six developmental stages of the Masterson Method. Exploring more than 15 of Masterson's volumes, as well as countless articles, Daws shows how Masterson's approach to Object Relations and the developmental self can serve clinicians in both conceptualising and treating borderline, narcissistic and schizoid disorders of self. Considering the pioneering and innovative nature of Masterson's work, Daws looks at how he creatively expanded on Freud's theories on repression, successfully developing therapeutically sound ways to touch and transform developmental trauma and trauma reflected in a deep abandonment depression. James F. Masterson: A Contemporary Introduction will be of interest to students in psychology, psychiatry and psychiatric nursing, as well as psychoanalytically orientated psychotherapists, psychoanalysts, and those specializing in the ever-growing field of the treatment of the disorders of the self"--cProvided by publisher.12aMasterson, James F.12aPsychoanalytic Theory22aPersonality Disorders 0aRoutledge introductions to contemporary psychoanalysis.  aAUTH02014pam a2200397 i 9918986651306676DNLM20251118111404.0230720s2024    flu      b    001 0 eng    a  2023030934  a9781032469676q(hbk)  a1032469676q(hbk)  a9781032471600q(pbk)  a1032471603q(pbk)  z9781003384823q(ebk)  a(OCoLC)1401628437  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdOCLCFdIG#  apcc  9United States00aRC627.54b.C87 202400aQU 26000a616.3/9223/eng/2023100200aCurrent trends in the diagnosis and management of metabolic disorders /cedited by Seth Kwabena Amponsah, Emmanuel Kwaku Ofori, Yashwant V. Pathak.  aFirst edition. 1aBoca Raton :bCRC Press,c2024.  axiv, 360 pages :billustrations ;c27 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  a"This volume provides an overview of the biochemical basis of metabolic diseases and molecular basis of chemical pathologies. Metabolic disorders occur when metabolic processes in the body are disrupted. They contribute a significant burden to human health globally. They can be congenital or acquired, for example, diabetes mellitus, obesity, metabolic syndrome, osteoporosis, osteopenia, mild-moderate hypovitaminosis D, erectile dysfunction, dyslipidemia, and thyroiditis. Metabolic disorders have gained significant importance due to the exponential increase in obesity worldwide. Early diagnosis of metabolic disorders is important in order to employ lifestyle and risk factor modification"--cProvided by publisher.12aMetabolic Diseases1 aAmponsah, Seth Kwabena,eeditor.1 aOfori, Emmanuel Kwaku,eeditor.1 aPathak, Yashwant,eeditor.  aAUTH01183cam a22003011  450000100100000000300050001000500170001500700140003200800410004603500200008704000210010704400110012806000190013910000350015824501500019325000130034326000300035630000150038633600260040133700280042733800270045550000570048253301100053954001420064958300630079170000180085499900090087261741180RDNLM20251118101108.0hd|bfa012baap820626s1901    onc||||  |||| 00| 0|eng    a(OCoLC)14783130  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9Canada00aQVbP436s 19011 aPereira, Jonathan,d1804-1853.10aSelecta è praescriptis.bSelections from physicians' prescriptions.  For the use of medical and pharmaceutical students.c[Ed. by Joseph Inge].  a18th ed.  aToronto,bCarveth,c1901.  axi, 364 p.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aNLM microfilm copy shelved as: Film 5583 no. 25DNLM  aMicrofilm.b[Bethesda, Md.] :cNational Library of Medicine,d1994.e1 microfilm reel : negative ; 35 mm.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill not digitizec20201123lPhysic