reproductive endocrinology and infertility /cPak H. Chung, Zev Rosenwaks, editors. 1aCham :bSpringer,c2023.  axv, 258 pages ;billustrations (some color) ;c24 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aContemporary Endocrinologyx2523-3785  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.0 aIntro -- Series Editor Foreword -- Preface -- Contents -- Contributors -- Chapter 1: Ambiguous Genitalia -- Differential Diagnosis -- Evaluation -- Treatment -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 2: Precocious Puberty -- Background -- Normal Pubertal Stages -- Differential Diagnosis of Precocious Puberty -- Evaluation [1, 3, 4] -- Treatment [1, 2] -- CPP -- PPP -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 3: Delayed Puberty -- Background -- Definition of Delayed Puberty -- Differential Diagnosis of Delayed Puberty -- Evaluation -- History and Physical Examination8 aLaboratory Investigation and Imaging -- Treatment -- Discussion -- Suggested Readings -- Chapter 4: Primary Amenorrhea -- Discussion -- Differential Diagnosis -- References -- Chapter 5: Secondary Amenorrhea -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 6: Mullerian Anomaly -- Differential Diagnosis -- Evaluation -- Treatment -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 7: Dysmenorrhea -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 8: Abnormal Uterine Bleeding -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 9: Hirsutism -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 10: Polycystic Ovarian Syndrome (PCOS) -- Discussion -- References8 aChapter 11: Hyperprolactinemia -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 12: Thyroid and Reproduction -- Discussion -- Interpretation of Thyroid Function Tests (TFTs) -- Iodine Supplementation for Pregnancy and Lactation -- Screening for Maternal Hypothyroidism -- Maternal Subclinical Hypothyroidism -- Thyroid Autoimmunity -- Maternal Hyperthyroidism: Diagnosis -- Maternal Hyperthyroidism: Treatment -- Postpartum Thyroiditis -- Summary -- References -- Chapter 13: Infertility Evaluation -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 14: Hypothalamic Hypogonadism -- Discussion -- References8 aChapter 15: Endometriosis and Infertility -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 16: Uterine Fibroids -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 17: Ovarian Cysts -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 18: Decreased Ovarian Reserve -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 19: Primary Ovarian Insufficiency -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 20: Tubal Factor -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 21: Endometrial Factor -- Discussion -- Intrauterine Pathology -- Thin Lining -- Endometrial Receptivity Analysis (ERA) -- Chronic Endometritis -- Conclusion -- References8 aChapter 22: Recurrent Pregnancy Loss -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 23: Evaluation of Male Infertility -- Discussion -- History -- Physical Exam -- Semen Analysis -- Laboratory Testing -- Genetic Testing -- Adjunctive Tests -- Imaging -- References -- Chapter 24: Erectile Dysfunction -- Discussion -- Pathophysiology -- Evaluation -- Treatment -- Lifestyle Changes -- Medications -- Phosphodiesterase 5 Inhibitors -- Vacuum Erection Device -- Intraurethral Alprostadil -- Intracavernosal Injections -- Surgery -- References -- Chapter 25: Varicocele -- Discussion -- History -- Semen Analysis -- Chapter 26: Azoospermia -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 27: Advanced Sperm Function Testing -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 28: Psychological Factors and Fertility Counseling -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 29: Intrauterine Insemination -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 30: Assisted Reproductive Technology -- Background -- Epidemiology -- Evaluation -- Treatment -- Discussion -- Conclusion -- References -- Suggested Readings -- Chapter 31: Ovarian Hyperstimulation Syndrome (OHSS) -- Evaluation -- Differential Diagnosis -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 32: Pre-Implantation Genetic Testing -- Discussion -- Reference -- Chapter 33: Planned Fertility Preservation -- Discussion -- References -- Chapter 34: Fertility Preservation: Medical -- Discussion -- Suggested Readings -- Chapter 35: Menopause -- Diagnosis -- Management -- Discussion -- References -- Index  aIn the vast majority of books discussing reproductive endocrinology and infertility (REI), the contents are organized and classified by organs and systems. In contrast, this book is problem-based: chapters are sensibly arranged according to the chief complaints from patients presenting at the office. Readers will be guided to formulate the differential diagnoses, select the appropriate evaluation scheme to arrive at the correct diagnosis, and finally decide on the recommended treatment for the particular condition. The range of both male and female REI conditions are presented here, providing the clinician with the tools to sort through the numerous and often similar complaints from patients to reach the best treatment strategy. Discussed here are issues of puberty, menstrual conditions, uterine anomalies, fibroids, endometriosis, male and female infertility, pregnancy loss, menopause and many others. Current diagnostic and treatment guidelines and algorithms for all conditions are included, further streamlining the management process. Written by experts from the Ronald O. Perelman and Claudia Cohen Center of Reproductive Medicine at Weill Medical College of Cornell University, a world-renowned group of reproductive physicians, Problem-Focused Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility is an indispensable resource for office-based management of REI conditions.12aGenital Diseases12aInfertility22aGonadal Disorders22aMenstruation Disturbances 2aCase Reports1 aChung, Pak H.,eeditor.1 aRosenwaks, Zev,eeditor. 0aContemporary endocrinology (Totowa, N.J.)x2523-3785.  aAUTH01726nam a2200457 i 9918986596106676DNLM20251124110429.0231122s2024    nyu           000 0deng    a1410104052  a9781613322352qpaperback  a1613322356qpaperback  a9781613322369qh