  a1391212658  a1529767342qhardback  a9781529767346qhardback  a9781529767339qpaperback  a1529767334qpaperback  a(OCoLC)1391212709z(OCoLC)1391212658  aYDXbengerdacYDXdOCLCQdOCLCLdYDXdOCLCOdYDXdSINLBdOCLCOdCDCdPZXdUKNEZdNNY  apcc  9England 4aRJ245b.E75 202400aWY 15904a618.920023122300aEssentials of nursing children and young people /cedited by Jayne Price, Orla McAlinden and Zoë Veal.  a2nd edition. 1aLondon ;aThousand Oaks, California :bSage Publications,c[2024] 4c©2024  axx, 650 pages :billustrations ;c25 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.00gPart 1: Principles of nursing children --tInvolving children, young people and families in care /rNicola Mitchell ; Joanna Smith ; Jackie Vasey --tEffective communication with children and young people /rOria McAlinden ; Jean Shapcott --tAssessment and management of pain in children and young people /rRebecca Saul ; Allison Twycross --tMedication: management, administration and compliance/concordance /rMary Brady ; Linda Moore --tInterprofessional working /rGeorgina Green --tOrganisation and settings for care of children and young people /rJane Hughes ; Amanda Kelly ; Tracey Jones ; Orla McAlinden --tCommunity care and care in non-hospital settings for children and young people /rGareth Jones ; Sarah Jones ; Orla McAlinden ; Jacqui Scrace --tLaw and policy for children and young people's nursing /rMarc Cornock --tSafeguarding children and young people /rCameron Cox ; Zoe Clark --gPart 2: Child and infant wellbeing and development --tGenetics and epigenetics: effects on children and young people /rGill Langmack ; Elisabeth O'Brien --tInfant mental wellbeing and health or 'how to grow a health adult' /rOrla McAlinden --tFactors influencing wellbeing and development in children and young people /rMelanie Robbins ; Cilla Sanders --tUniversal screening and the role of the health visitor /rMandy Brimble ; Sarah Reddington-Bowes --gPart 3: Caring for children and young people with acute healthcare needs and injury --tAssessment and care of children and young people with acute needs /rRachel Bolland --tPreparing children and young people for hospitalisation /rMicky Varley ; Elena Higginson --tCare of children and young people in the peri- and postoperative recovery period /rKaren Pattrick --tCare of children and young people with respiratory problems /rZ<U+fffd>o Veal ; Orla McAlinden ; Doreen Crawford --tCare of children and young people with cardiovascular problems /rJo Bailey ; Zoë Veal --tCare of children and young people with neurological problems /rStuart Hibbins --tCare of children with urinary and renal problems /rMary Brady ; Linda Moore --tCare of children and young people with endocrine problems /rKate Davies --tCare of children and young people with immunological problems /rKatie Warburton --tCare of children and young people with musculoskeletal problems /rJulia Judd --tCare of children and young people with haematological problems /rLizzy Hoole --tCare of children and young people with a thermal injury /rShirin Pomeroy --tCare of children and young people with fluid and electrolyte imbalance /rZ<U+fffd>o Veal ; Colin Veal --tCare of children and young people with gastrointestinal problems /rZoë Veal ; Rebekah Overend ; Doreen Crawford --tDischarge planning and transfer for children and young people /rElizabeth Gillespie ; Jane Price --gPart 4: Caring for children and young people with complex and high dependency needs --tCare of highly dependent and critically ill children and young people /rUsha Chandran ; Fiona Lynch --tCare of the neonate /rKathleen Mangahis ; Catharine Grob --tCare of children and young people with a malignant condition /rJayne Price ; Suzanne Coulson --tCare of children and young people with life-limiting illness /rAntoinette Menezes ; Tracie Lewin-Taylor ; Jayne Price --tCare of children and young people at the end of life /rJayne Price ; Melissa Heywood --tCare of children and young people with learning disabilities /rTrish Griffin ; Jane Lopez --tCare of children and young people with mental health issues /rLaurence Baldwin ; Ann Cox --gPart 5: On being a professional children's nurse --tLeadership and management in children and young people's nursing /rMelanie Hayward --tLifelong learning and continuing professional development in children and young people's nursing /rClaire Anderson --tDecision-making and accountability in children and young people's nursing /rLorraine Highe.  a"This book maps to the content of the majority of pre-registration child nursing programmes, and by adopting a 5 part structure it clearly covers the core parts of training and practice that you will need: Part 1): Principles of nursing children and young people; Part 2): Wellbeing and development; Part 3): Caring for children and young people with acute health care needs and injury; Part 4): Caring for children and young people with complex and high dependency needs; Part 5): Being a professional children and young people's nurse" -- From publisher's website.12aNursing Carexmethods12aChild22aFamily Nursingxmethods22aAdolescent1 aPrice, Jayne,eeditor.1 aMcAlinden, Orlac(Nurse)eeditor.1 aVeal, Zoë,eeditor.  aAUTH00907nam a2200301 i 45000010017000000030005000170050017000220080041000390200018000800400025000980420008001230440011001310600014001421000032001562450063001882500019002512640039002703000056003093360026003653370028003913380027004195040041004466100049004876500023005366500026005596510011005859990009005969918803678406676DNLM20251118163223.0240417s2021    bl ac    b    000 0 por    a9786599158544  aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  apcc  9Brazil00aWX 28 DB81 aTavares, Zózimo,eauthor.10aHGV :bum marco na saúde do Piauí /cZózimo Tavares.  a1a ediçâo. 1aTeresina :bBienal Editora,c2021.  a178 pages :billustrations, portraits ;c20 x 20 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references.22aHospital Getúlio Vargas (Teresina, Brazil)12aHospitalsxhistory22aHistory, 20th Century 2aBrazil  aAUTH01855nam a2200433 i 9918843681506676DNLM20251120082537.0240625s2024    sp a     b    000 0 spa    a  2023378655  a9788449342271q(paperback)  a8449342279  a(OCoLC)1443081396  aSP-BaPLbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdIG#dNZAUCdOCLCO  alccopycatapcc  ae-sp---  9Spain00aRD592.9.M38bA3 202400aWL 36804a617.480922231 aMartín-Fernández, Jesús,d1992-eauthor.10aDime qué sientes :bdiario de un neurocirujano : pacientes despiertos, las 5 dimensiones del cerebro y un cambio de paradigma /cJesús Martín-Fernández.  a1a. edición. 1aBarcelona, España :bPaidós,cabril de 2024.  a255 pages, 4 unnumbered pages of plates :billustrations (some color) ;c24 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aPaidós contextos  aIncludes bibliographical references.  a"En febrero de 2023, el doctor Jesús Martín-Fernández llevó a cabo, con éxito, la primera cirugía cerebral despierta en la que utilizó un test de inteligencia artificial para identificar y preservar las emociones del paciente. Con este hito, no solo revoluciona la medicina actual, sino que abre la puerta a nuevas y fascinantes teorías sobre el órgano más misterioso del cuerpo humano, el cerebro."--Back cover.12aBrainxsurgery22aNeurosurgical Proceduresxmethods22aCraniotomyxmethods22aWakefulness22aBrain Mapping 2aCase Reports 0aPaidós contextos  aAUTH04971nam a2200433 i 9918917738006676DNLM20251114125002.0191118s2019    fr a     b    000 0 fre    a  2020366045  a9782705697723q(paperback)  a2705697721  a(OCoLC)1137150094  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCFdPULdYUSdOCLCOdOCLCLdOCLCQ  apcc  9France00aRA779b.L53 201900aWZ 29004a618.1qOCoLC1 aLeroy, Alphonse Vincent Louis Antoine,d1741?-1816,eauthor.10aRecherches sur les habillemens des femmes et des enfans10aRecherches sur les habillemens des femmes et des enfans, ou, Examen de la manière dont il faut vêtir l'un & l'autre sèxe /cAlphonse Leroy ; édité par Hélène Cazes et Frédéric Charbonneau.30aExamen de la manière dont il faut vêtir l'un & l'autre sèxe3 aExamen de la manière dont il faut vêtir l'un et l'autre sèxe 1aParis :bHermann,c[2019]  a188 pages :billustrations ;c23 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aRépublique des lettres. Sources  aIncludes bibliographical references (pages 181-186).00g1.tCombien il importe au Gouvernement de s'occuper de l'Enfance --g2.tÉtat & besoins d'un enfant qui vient de naître --g3.tDes différentes manières de vêtir les enfans au sortir du sein de leur mère --g4.tRecherches sur l'antiquité des maillots, & sur les avantages qui ont pû contribuer à conserver leur usage --g5.tDe la nécessité d'abandonner l'usage des maillots --g6.tRéforme à faire dans la manière d'habiller & de coucher les enfans --g7.tInconvéniens des béguins & têtieres --g8.tDe la tête en général, & des usages des divers peuples relativement à cette partie --g9.tCe qui doit s'observer relativement à la tête des enfans --g10.tComment tout ce qui gêne l'accroissement des enfans, s'oppose au développement de leur esprit, & comment tout ce qui développe trop tôt leur esprit s'oppose à leur accroissement --g1.tDifférences notables entre l'homme, la femme & les enfans --g2.tCombien sont contraires à la santé la plûpart des vêtemens communs & particuliers à l'un &à l'autre sèxe --g3.tDe l'origine des corps & de leurs différentes espèces --g4.tDu danger des corps en général --g5.tDanger des corps, relativement à la respiration --g6.tDanger des corps, relativement à la nutrition --g7.tDanger des corps, relativement à l'accouchement --g8.tCombien les corps nuisent à la beauté --g9.tRecherches sur les causes qui ont pû concourir à établir l'usage des corps --g1.tExamen de quelques conformations vicieuses causées par les vêtemens --g2.tMoyens de remédier aux difformités produites par les vêtemens --g3.tDe l'origine & de l'utilité des ceintures --g4.tQuelle doit être la manière de se vêtir dans les différentes circonstances à- dans les différens âges de la vie --g5.tComment les Vêtemens ont concouru, avec d'autres causes, à la dégénérescence, & quels seroient les moyens d'y remédier.  a"Alphonse Leroy (1742-1816), bien connu de ses contemporains comme médecin aux opinions tranchées et tranchantes, commença une prolixe carrière d'écrivain médical avec ces Recherches sur les habillemens des femmes et des enfans. Dans cet ouvrage, il rassemble remarques, préceptes, exposés techniques et envolées lyriques à propos de la petite enfance, de l'anatomie, de la nature humaine, de la force de caractère et du danger des modes. Le vêtement, des langes au corset, en passant par la ceinture et le bonnet, lui paraît en effet au coeur des pratiques sociales ; cette protection du corps devient un péril lorsque les conventions contredisent la nature. La "nouvelle révolution", que guide Leroy, apportera le bonheur à tous : le jeune médecin dénonce la perversion des contraintes vestimentaires pour mieux persuader ses lecteurs d'une nécessaire réforme de leurs pratiques. Le projet de Leroy soulève les questions de son époque sur la nature, la famille et la santé publique. Le nouveau-né peut-il survivre sans des soins éclairés par la médecine ? Les habitudes sociales nuisent-elles à l'organisme ? Le médecin a-t-il pour rôle d'éduquer la société ? Lui seul en effet connaîtrait tout autant la nature que les usages et les mirages de la culture."--Page 4 of cover.12aClothing22aSocial Norms1 aCazes, Hélène,eeditor.1 aCharbonneau, Frédéric,d1967-eeditor. 0aCollections de la République des lettres.pSources  aAUTH01114pam a2200325 i 9918991788906676DNLM20251114085253.0240407s2024    sz a     b    000 0 eng    a9783031600609qpaperback  a3031600606qpaperback  z9783031600616qebook  a(OCoLC)1428894790  aUKMGBbengerdacUKMGBdOCLCO  apcc  9Switzerland00aQV 7781 aSilva, Ana Catarinac(Of Universidade do Porto),eauthor.10aBiotechnology for pharmaceutical sciences :bconcepts and applications /cAna Catarina Silva. 1aCham, Switzerland :bSpringer,c[2024]  avii, 94 pages :billustrations ;c24 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aSpringerBriefs in molecular science,x2192-5407  aIncludes bibliographical references.12aTechnology, Pharmaceutical22aBiological Products 0aSpringerBriefs in molecular sciencex2192-5407  aAUTH01413cas a2200409 i 9918840888906676DNLM20251113142306.0m     o  d        cr#|||||||||||240117c20249999enk|| poo     0    0eng    a  2025227943  a1420244224  a2976-9337l2976-9337  a(OCoLC)1423153942z(OCoLC)1420244224  aSFBbengerdad20251113cSFBdOCLKBdDNLM  apcc  9England00aW110aRadiol Adv2dnlm00aRadiology advances. 1a[Oxford] :bOxford University Press,c[2024]-  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Volume 1, issue 1 (May 2024).0 aPubMedbv1n1, 2024-0 aPMC  aDescription based on: Volume 1, issue 1 (May 2024); title from journal contents homepage (Oxford Academic website, viewed September 16, 2024).  aLatest issue consulted: Volume 2, issue 1 (January 2025) (viewed March 17, 2025).12aRadiology 2aPeriodical2 aRadiological Society of North America,eissuing body.40uhttps://academic.oup.com/radadv/issue40uhttps://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/journals/?term=9918840888