ölmerich, Jürgen  aAUTH01428cas a2200433 a 9616288DNLM20251126115233.0cr|cn#||||||||981016d19962019gw ar         0    0ger    a  2004243085  a1430-9017l1430-9017  a(DNLM)SR0089791(s)  a(OCoLC)38298236  aOSUcOSUdOCLdNLMdDNLM0 ageraeng  alcdanlmcopyc  9Germany00aW1bJA2017  aBJ57b.J3410aJahr Wiss Ethik2dnlm00aJahrbuch für Wissenschaft und Ethik.  aBerlin ;aNew York :bWalter de Gruyter,cc1996-2019  av. ;c23 cm.  aAnnual  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aBd. 1 (1996)-1 aCeased with Volume 24, issue 1 (July 2019).  aLatest issue consulted: Bd. 7 (2002).0 aMEDLINEbSelected citations only0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online.  aArticles in German; text of documents in English and German.  3Vol. 1 (1996)c19961002fNotice publishedlPrinted on acid-free paper that meets the full ANSI standard for Permanent Paper12aSciencexethics4 uhttps://www.degruyter.com/view/j/jfwe?recentIssue=true  aAUTH03430cam a2200433 i 9918986638506676DNLM20251128072253.0230928t20242024njua     b    001 0 eng    a  2023032749  a9781394229239q(paperback)  a1394229232q(paperback)  z9781394229253q(adobe pdf)  z9781394229246q(epub)  a(OCoLC)1413441851  aDLCbengerdad20251128dOCLCOdOCLCLdOCLCFdYDXdOCLCOdIULdOCLCOdIG#041dDNLM  apcc  9United States00aRC394.W6bM38 202400aWL 340.600a616.85/53223/eng/202312111 aMather, Nancy,eauthor.10aEssentials of dyslexia assessment and intervention /cNancy Mather, Barbara J. Wendling.  aSecond edition. 1aHoboken, New Jersey :bWiley,c[2024] 4c©2024  axi, 388 pages :billustrations ;c28 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aEssentials of psychological assessment series  aRevised edition of: Essentials of dyslexia assessment and intervention / Nancy Mather and Barbara J. Wendling. c2012.  aIncludes bibliographical references (pages 345-372) and index.00tUnderstanding dyslexia --tA brief history of dyslexia --tThe brain and dyslexia /rDeborah Schneider, Fumiko Hoeft, Nancy Mather, Barbara Wendling, Sally Shaywitz, and Bennett Shaywitz --tGenetics and the environment /rDeborah Schneider, Nancy Mather, and Barbara J. Wendling --tAssessment of cognitive and linguistic risk factors --tAssessment of decoding, encoding, and reading fluency --tPhonological awareness and early reading and spelling --tOrthography and orthographic mapping for reading and spelling /rNancy Redding, Nancy Mather, and Barbara J. Wendling --tTeaching the orthographic system by integrating morphology, etymology, and phoneme-grapheme relationships /rSue Scibetta Hegland --tInstruction in basic reading skills and spelling --tInstruction in reading fluency --tTechnology applications for students with dyslexia /rKathleen Puckett --tDyslexia in different languages and English learners /rMartha Youman and Emily Mather --tDyslexia in the schools --gAppendix A.tDescriptions of tests --gAppendix B.tDescriptions of evidence-based programs --gAppendix C.tMobile apps and websites to support reading and writing instruction /rElaine Cheesman.  a"Dyslexia is a specific type of developmental reading disorder in which problems exist in basic reading skills, reading fluency, and spelling. These problems typically emerge early in a child's educational history, are persistent, and are unexpected given an individual's overall cognitive abilities and instructional experiences. Most researchers estimate that as many as 5 to 8% of students have dyslexia, whereas several professionals and professional organizations state that the prevalence may be as high as 20%. (e.g., Shaywitz & Shaywitz, 2020). All educational professionals need to have an understanding of dyslexia and its impact on reading, spelling, and emotional development"--cProvided by publisher.12aDyslexia1 aWendling, Barbara J.,eauthor. 0aEssentials of psychological assessment series.  aAUTH02540nam a2200385 i 9918842988206676DNLM20251120064718.0250220s2023    ag a     b    000 0 spa    a1504406148  a9789502334004  a9502334000  a(OCoLC)1504405910  aARFGCbengerdacARFGCdOCLCOdCGU  apcc  9Argentina 4aRA425b.B73 202300aWA 1001 aBrangold, Mauro,eauthor.10aAprehender salud pública :besquemas para aprender, enseñar y comprender /cMauro Brangold.  aPrimera edición. 1aCiudad de Buenos Aires :bEUDEBA,coctubre de 2023.  a471 pages :billustrations ;c24 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aManuales  aIncludes bibliographical references.00aCapítulo 1. Salud y determinantes -- Capítulo 2. La salud pública -- Capítulo 3. Derecho de la salud -- Capítulo 4. Promoción de la salud y prevención de enfermedades -- Capítulo 5. Indicadores en salud -- Capítulo 6. Demografía -- Capítulo 7. Investigación en ciencias de la salud -- Capítulo 8. Epidemiología.  aThe present work by Dr. Mauro Brangold constitutes a highly relevant contribution in the field of teaching dedicated to public health. The knowledge developed is approached from a systemic perspective, based on population studies, and encompasses both a field of knowledge and one of action. Supported by a series of explanatory diagrams, serving as a conceptual summary--of great andragogical and didactic value--the author presents content from the so-called "public health sciences," such as epidemiology and demography. He proposes spaces for reflection on the meaning of certain terms and challenges traditional theoretical frameworks, providing updates and integration into the domains of learning. The work encourages students to engage in the arduous task of bibliographic research and, in the assignments derived from practical work, motivates them to immerse themselves in the methodology of health research. Additionally, it provides educators with a valuable set of teaching tools, with the purpose of illustrating and enriching learning environments.12aPublic Health22aHealth Services22aHealth Services Research 0aManuales (Editorial Universitaria de Buenos Aires)  aAUTH01441cam a2200361 i 07210080RDNLM20251120134911.0hd|bfa012baap810725s1912    nyu      b    001 0 eng    a(OCoLC)14804297  aDNLMbengerdad20251120dDNLM  9United States00aQT 150bB628a 19121 aBlackham, Robert J.q(Robert James),d1868-1951,eauthor.10aAids to tropical hygiene /cby Major R.J. Blackham. 1aNew York :bWilliam Wood & Company,cMDCCCCXII [1912]  avii, 192 pages, 1 unnumbered folded leaf ;c16 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aStudents' aids series  aNLM microfilm copy shelved as: Film 12238, no. 25DNLM  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  aMicrofilm.b[Bethesda, Md.] :cNational Library of Medicine,d2003.e1 microfilm reel : negative ; 35 mm.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202011062pda5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20251120lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM12aHygiene22aPublic Health22aTropical Climate 0aStudents' aids series  aAUTH01434nam a2200373 i 101772314DNLM20251114151940.0201013r18891889nyu      b    000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5499 no.261 aLydston, G. Frankq(George Frank),d1858-1923eauthor.10aApparent cancerous transformation of syphiloma of the tongue :bexcision of the tongue by the galvano-cautery /cby G. Frank Lydston. 1a[New York] :b[publisher not identified],c[1889]  a16 pages ;c22 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aCaption title.  a"Reprint from N. Y. Medical record, Oct. 26, 1889."  a"NLM copy, author's presentation copy.5DNLM  aIncludes bibl