nnumbered leaf of plates :billustrations (color) ;c22 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aCaption title.  a"From the American journal of science and arts, Vol. XIX, No. 2."  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202504075DNLM12aArsenic Poisoningxdiagnosis22aArsenicxanalysis22aArsenicalsxanalysis22aClinical Chemistry Testsxmethods22aForensic Toxicology0 aAmerican journal of science and arts.  aAUTH02465nam a2200409 i 9918986649006676DNLM20251113114232.0230803t20242024enka     b    001 0 eng    a  2023027676  a9781032483986qhardcover  a1032483989qhardcover  a9781032478968qpaperback  a1032478969qpaperback  z9781003388838qelectronic book  a(OCoLC)1394065366  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdOCLCFdYDXdOCLCO  apcc  9England00aRC506b.M65 202400aWM 460.600a616.89/17223/eng/202308171 aMolinari, Elena,d1960-eauthor.10aBinocular vision :ban inquiry into psychoanalytic techniques and field theory /cElena Molinari. 1aAbingdon, Oxon ;aNew York, NY :bRoutledge, Taylor & Francis Group,c2024. 4c©2024  axii, 184 pages :billustrations ;c25 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  a"Binocular Vision in Psychoanalysis explains field theory from a Bionian perspective, while exploring the relationship between art and psychoanalysis. Elena Molinari starts from Bion's double definition to explore the relationship between the conscious and unconscious thought process. She looks at a wide range of specific situations where field theory can be beneficial, from mother-baby therapy with a borderline mother, couple and group therapy, and the relationship of female subjectivity between an analyst and an adolescent analysand. In each situation, Molinari unpicks what Binocular Vision might mean as a transformative process used to explore the primitive parts of the mind. By doing so, she brings the reader back to the earliest developments of the primary relationship between analyst and client, and how this process can unite the psychoanalytic process and the artistic process. The book has been written for psychotherapists approaching and utilising field theory in child and adult psychoanalysis, and offers vital knowledge to clinicians working with patients in primitive states"--cProvided by publisher.12aPsychoanalytic Therapy22aProfessional-Patient Relations.22aUnconscious, Psychology22aConsciousness  aAUTH02187cgm a22003974a 9806354DNLM20240607210935.0vf|cbahou980702s1998    xxu057| ||||| ||||vueng  42aFFH 7683bFilms for the Humanities & Sciences  a(OCoLC)39656088  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9United States00aWM 270bVC no.144 199804aThe next generation /ca presentation of Films for the Humanities & Sciences ; a production of Public Affairs Television, Inc. ; a presentation of Thirteen/WNET New York.  aPrinceton, N.J. :bFilms for the Humanities & Sciences,cc1998.  a1 videocassette (57 min.) :bsd., col. ;c1/2 in.  atwo-dimensional moving imagebtdi2rdacontent  avideobv2rdamedia  avideocassettebvf2rdacarrier1 aClose to home  aExecutive editors, Bill Moyers, Judith Davidson Moyers.8 a(Producer)  Experts are increasingly focusing on prevention efforts based on community and family.  This documentary looks at two of these efforts.  One works with parents addicted to heroin by teaching them how to repair the damage to family wrought by drug abuse, and in spite of it, how to raise strong, resilient children.  In a second program, vigilant counselors in Dade County schools watch for kids at risk of becoming drug addicts, and offer immediate counseling for those who are already involved with drugs.  Nicotine addiction is addressed by a program that provides classes designed to prevent students from smoking, and another that helps them stop if they've already begun to smoke.  School officials, counselors, and students are interviewed.12aSubstance-Related Disordersxprevention & control22aAdolescent22aChild of Impaired Parents22aSubstance-Related Disorders.22aSubstance-Related Disordersxtherapy 2aPersonal Narrative1 aMoyers, Bill,d1934-2025.2 aFilms for the Humanities (Firm) 0aClose to home (Series)  aHISRELb19991201  aAUTH01290nam a2200325 i 9918988295806676DNLM20251113111835.0250205s2025    ag a     b    001 0 spa    a9788411061445q(versión impresa + versión digital)  z9788411061452q(versión digital)  aDNLMbengerdacDNLM  apcc  9Argentina00aWS 350.600aPsiquiatría infantil y de la adolescencia /cdirectores, Pedro Javier Rodríguez-Hernández, Amaia Hervás Zúñiga ; coordinadores, Abigail Huertas Patón, Ma. Inmaculada Palanca Maresca, Matías Real López ; miembro del comité editorial, María Jesús Mardomingo Sanz. 1aBuenos Aires :bEditorial Médica Panamericana,c[2025]  axvii, 657 pages :billustrations ;c28 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical reference and index.12aMental Disorders12aChild Psychiatryxmethods22aAdolescent Psychiatryxmethods22aChild22aAdolescent1 aRodríguez-Hernández, Pedro Javier,eeditor.1 aHervás Zúñiga, Amaia,eeditor.  aAUTH01233cas a2200385 i 9918400088606676DNLM20251125073419.0220504c20029999gw qr p       0    0ger    a  2025228040  a1869-7712l1869-7712  a(OCoLC)1552757836  aDNLMbengerdad20251124dDNLM0 agerbeng  apcc  9Germany00aW1bZE625T00aZeitschrift für Transaktionsanalyse.1 aZTA 1aPaderborn :bJunfermann-Verlag,c[2002]-  avolumes  aFour times a year  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aBegan with Jahrg. 19, Heft 1 (2002)  a