ia, Giovanni,eauthor.14aMaciocia's the practice of Chinese medicine :bthe treatment of diseases with acupuncture and Chinese herbs /cGiovanni Maciocia ; third edition foreword by Michael McIntyre.1 aPractice of Chinese medicine  aThird edition. 1aSt. Louis, Missouri :bElsevier,c[2022] 4c©2022  axxiv, 1290 pages :bcolor illustrations ;c25 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aTitle in Chinese on cover: 中藥針灸治療學.  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.00tAbdominal Masses --tAbdominal Pain --tAcid Reflux (Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease)--tAllergic Rhinitis--tAnxiety--tAsthma (Allergic Asthma & Atopic Eczema)--tAtrophy Syndrome--tBenign Prostatic Hyperplasia--tBleeding--tBreathlessness--tChest Painful Obstruction Syndrome--tChronic Fatigue Syndrome--tCommon Cold and Influenza--tConstipation--tCough--tDepression--tDiarrhea--tDizziness--tEmotions (The)--tEnuresis and Incontinence--tEpigastric Pain--tErectile Dysfunction--tFibromyalgia--tGoitre (Thyroid Problems)--tHeadaches--tHypertension--tHypochondrial Pain--tInsomnia--tInterstitial Cystitis--tLower Back Ache--tMental-Emotional Problems – Aetiology --tMental-Emotional Problems – Diagnosis --tMental-Emotional Problems – Patterns and their Treatment--tMouth Ulcers--tMultiple Sclerosis--tNausea/Vomiting--tOedema (Edema) --tPainful Obstruction Syndrome--tParkinson’s Disease--tProstatitis--tPsyche (The) in Chinese Medicine--tSinusitis--tTinnitus--tTiredness--tUrinary Retention--tUrinary Syndrome--tWheezing--tWind-Stroke.  aUse Traditional Chinese Medicine in diagnosing and treating disease! Maciocia’s The Practice of Chinese Medicine, 3rd Edition describes how to apply TCM theory to the diagnosis and treatment of disorders and conditions frequently encountered in practice. Covering common, chronic, and acute conditions, Maciocia’s provides guidelines to treatment with both acupuncture and Chinese herbs. Case studies offer real-world insights into determining effective treatment care. From an expert team of editors who were close to the late Giovanni Maciocia and who practice "the Maciocia way," this practical, illustrated text makes it easier to apply TCM in Western medical practice.12aMedicine, Chinese Traditionalxmethods22aAcupuncture Therapyxmethods22aPhytotherapyxmethods1 aMcIntyre, Michael,d1946-ewriter of foreword.  aAUTH01245nam a2200325 i 101776518DNLM20251119102107.0210225r18831883nyu           000 0 eng    aDNLMbengerdacDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW6bP3 v.7481 box 5509 no.161 aSutton, R. S.q(Rhoades Stansbury),d1841-1906eauthor.14aThe importance of cleanliness in surgical operations /cby R. Stansbury Sutton. 1a[New York?] :b[publisher not identified],c[1883]  a13 pages ;c23 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aCover title.  a"Reprint from Volume III, Gynecological transactions. 1883."  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202504072pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202504075DNLM12aWound Infectionxprevention & control22aAnti-Infective Agents, Local22aDrainage22aGerm Theory of Disease0 aGynecological transactions.  aAUTH01492cam a2200349 i 08120720RDNLM20251120134046.0hd|bfa012baap810725s1906    pauaf         001 0 eng    a(OCoLC)14810126  aDNLMbengerdad20251120dDNLM  9United States00aQU 25bR684L 19061 aRockwood, Elbert W.q(Elbert William),d1860-1935,eauthor.12aA laboratory manual of physiological chemistry /cby Elbert W. Rockwood.  aSecond edition, revised and enlarged. 1aPhiladelphia :bF. A. Davis Company,c1906.  aix, 229 pages, IV leaves of plates :billustrations (some color) ;c19 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes index.  a"With one colored plate and three plates of microscopic preparations."  aNLM microfilm copy shelved as: Film 12276 no. 25DNLM  aMicrofilm.bBethesda, Md. :cNational Library of Medicine,d2005.e1 microfilm reel: negative ; 35 mm.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202011062pda5DNLM  aCondition reviewedc20251120lconservation not necessary2pda5DNLM12aBiochemical Phenomena 2aLaboratory Manual  aAUTH01233cam a2200301 i 450000100100000000300050001000500170001500800410003203500220007304000350009504400100013006000200014010000470016024501940020726400850040130000230048633600260050933700280053533800270056350000200059054001420061058300390075258300430079165100100083465500180084470000600086299900090092261860750RDNLM20251118144845.0820626s1905    cl            001 0 spa    a(OCoLC)1225182871  aDNLMbengerdad20251118dDNLM  9Chile00aQVAbP978f 19051 aPuga Borne, Federico,d1855-1935,eauthor.10aFarmacopea chilen ;bobra aprobada por la Facultad de Medicina y Farmacia de Chile y mandada adoptar por el Supremo Gobierno como farmacopea nacional /cpor F. Puga Borne y Juan B. Miranda. 1aSantiago de Chile :bImprenta, Litografía y Encuadernación Barcelona,c1905.  a393 pages ;c27 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes index.  aThe National Library of Medicine believes this item to be in the public domain.uhttps://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/5DNLM  aWill digitizec202011232pda5DNLM  aNeeds condition reviewc202011235DNLM 2aChile 2aPharmacopoeia1 aMiranda, Juan B.q(Juan Bautista),d1857-1920,eauthor.  aAUTH03370cam a22004214a 101054313DNLM20240608165212.0921202s1992    et a     bs  i000 0 eng    a   99894426   a(DNLM)PIP:00213004  a(OCoLC)38088161  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  apcc  9Ethiopia00aHQ 12bY12f 1992  a0728201 aYacob Zewoldi.10aFertility behaviour of elites and their perception of the population problem in Ethiopia :ba synthesis /cby Yacob Zewoldi.  aAddis Ababa, Ethiopia :bPublished for the Family Guidance Association of Ethiopia by United Nations Economic Commission for Africa,c[1992]  ax, 80 p. :bill.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references (p. 67-70).3 aThe results of a 1990 survey among lawyers, women's groups, government officials, teachers, physicians, and religious leaders living in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia to determine fertility behavior of the elites and their perception of rapid population growth are presented.  Knowledge of family planning (FP) was rather high (80-100%), but quite low among the Orthodox Christian leaders (24%).  Yet 80% of Muslim leaders knew about FP as well as all women.  Women's groups provided much information about FP.  The various groups interpreted FP to mean limiting family size and spacing births.  Ever-use of an FP method among ever-married elites was high in the nonreligious groups (range 68-95%), low for Muslim leaders (36%), and extremely low for Orthodox Christian leaders (5%).  Most elites expressed disapproval of abortion (100% of Orthodox Christians to 61% of university lecturers).  The age at 1st marriage ranged from 14.6 years for the wives of Orthodox Christian leaders to 24.9 years for university lecturers.  Adjusted mean number of children was highest among Muslim leaders (4.82) followed by artists (4.08) and women's groups (4.02).  University lecturers and physicians had the lowest fertility (3.24 and 3.13, respectively).  Desired family size varied from 9.62 for Muslim leaders to 3.32 for lawyers.  Most all groups recognized that the population was growing too quickly (61-93%).  Yet 60% of Orthodox Christian leaders felt the current growth rate was good, mainly because it was God's will.  Leaders who believed the growth rate was bad thought government should create public awareness of the population problem, introduce FP, create job opportunities, and devise a population policy.  Except for religious leaders (4% of Orthodox Christians and 32% of Muslims), the groups tended to note the link between population growth and environmental deterioration (91-97%).  Yet most everyone agreed that population and family life education should be introduced in high school (88-100%).12aPopulation Growth12aSexual Behavior22aData Collection22aFamily Planning Services22aMarriage22aSocioeconomic Factors. 2aEthiopia 2aStatistics2 aYaʼItyopyā bétasab mamriyā māhbar.2 aUnited Nations.bEconomic Commission for Africa.  aPIPRELb19921202  aAUTH01039cas a22003734a 101278197DNLM20251126101942.0cr|cn ||||||||060602c20069999enkbr p       0    0eng    a  2006244119  a1746-9899l1746-9899  a(OCoLC)77498363  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  alcd  9England00aW1bEX520Nk10aExpert Rev Ophthalmol2dnlm00aExpert review of ophthalmology.  aLondon, UK :bFuture Drugs Ltd.,cc2006-313June 2013- :aLondon :bInforma Healthcare  av. :bill.  aBimonthly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aVol. 1, no. 1 (Oct. 2006)-0 aPubMedbSelected citations only  aAlso issued online.12aEye Diseases 2aPeriodical0 x1746-99024 uhttp://www.tandfonline.com/loi/ierl20  aAUTH01566cas a2200469 a 8805645DNLM20251126100941.0cr|cn#||||||||880512c19889999mauqr p       0    0eng    a0891-9887l0891-9887  aJGPNEN  a(DNLM)SR0059706(s)  a(OCoLC)15051229  aDNLMcDNLMdDNLM  9United States00aW1bJO669ND10aJ Geriatr Psychiatry Neurol2dnlm 0aJournal of geriatric psychiatry and neurology00aJournal of geriatric psychiatry and neurology.  a[Littleton, MA] :bPSG Pub. Co.,c[c1988-3 aThousand Oaks, CA :bSage Publications  av. :bill.  aQuarterly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  